 I've only ascended 6 characters (V,S,A) and have had tons more
go down in flames. For me the "easy" levels are the ones I'm least
likely to rip through (well, I do try to, but inevitably get crushed).
It's the opposite, usually the higher levels are the easier ones as 
you're set by that point. If you can make it to the quest and have
picked up some sort of reflection (or gained all the intrinsics) so as
to deal with that damn stone giant hanging around with a wand of death
(or a gnome or elf with a wand of sleep for that matter), then
you should be okay. 

  For me, the most dangerous area by far is the gnomish mines. I'll either
jump right in and get trashed, or wait around and then be forced
to flee to them due to the annual "hill orc convention" up around
level 4 or 5. I've never lost a character that's made it through the quest,
but I've lost a boatload of them a level or so below the mine town.

 This isn't to say that the higher, or rather deeper levels of the game
are a breeze, but "instant death" should be more easily avoided.


